{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06CZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset U'$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$y'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$U'$", "MATH_0011": "$x$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0013": "$U$", "MATH_0014": "$\\gamma : p(x) \\to y'|_U$", "MATH_0015": "$x'$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0017": "$U'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\beta : x'|_U \\to x$", "MATH_0019": "$\\gamma' : p(x') \\to y'$", "MATH_0020": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-formally-smooth}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\np(x'|_U) \\ar[d]_{p(\\beta)} \\ar[rr]_{\\gamma'|_U} & &\ny'|_U \\ar@{=}[d] \\\\\np(x) \\ar[rr]^\\gamma & & y'|_U\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0021": "$(x', \\beta, \\gamma')$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:71f3b124b95f61fb19a291f9dd56d026f3621dcccf02afa7561516655f01f618", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53c3aa6d20f98aeed1083c17d02dd0c9d5ed05c82e4338d784ed0ac754a002a2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism\nof categories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0004>. We will say that\n<MATH_0005> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>formally smooth on objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the following condition holds:\nGiven any data consisting of\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> a first order thickening <MATH_0006> of affine schemes over <MATH_0007>,\n<STRUCT_0004> an object <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0005> an object <MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013>, and\n<STRUCT_0006> an isomorphism <MATH_0014>,\n<STRUCT_0007>\nthen there exists an object <MATH_0015> of\n<MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017> with an isomorphism\n<MATH_0018> and an isomorphism <MATH_0019>\nsuch that\n<MATH_0020>\ncommutes.  In this situation we say that ``<MATH_0021>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>solution<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> to the problem posed by our data (1), (2), (3), (4)''.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f5d5dc5784d173aa954d7427fa9c33fc39eac352454422e470c1c9460510d4f", "unit_id": "tag:06CZ:prose-0001"}
